text:
{
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "work-706-granted-map-fix",
      "summary": "#706 granted-map nil-panic fix — PR #707 OPEN, CI green, Copilot 1 comment fixed+replied, merge-ready. Unblocks rpg-api #598. ~5-line LoadFromData fix (data.go: re-init Granted, make() when nil after omitempty round-trip) + regression test (verified it panics without the fix).",
      "added": "2026-06-01"
    },
    {
      "id": "work-705-reshape-SURFACED",
      "summary": "Kirk flagged #705 TurnStateChangedEvent: turn-state/economy/menu are RULEBOOK concepts (rulebooks/dnd5e/character) genericized into the agnostic encounter/events spine — mislayers + discards the type. Same on EconomyConsumed (#698). SURFACED reshape analysis to director, did NOT implement. CRUX evidence: encounter pkg is dnd5e-coupled TODAY (11 source files import rulebooks/dnd5e); only encounter/events sub-pkg is agnostic; broker codec type-switches on events.* concretes. Fully-agnostic encounter is a SEPARATE goal (my prompt). So flattening rulebook types into events to keep events agnostic while the rest of encounter is coupled = inconsistent half-measure. MY READ: option (a) carry the rulebook type directly via a generic typed-payload envelope (event = {kind, actorID, payload json.RawMessage}; dnd5e marshals ActorTurnState in, host routes by kind) — keeps the spine's transport agnostic without genericizing/discarding the rulebook type; also fixes EconomyConsumed consistently. Option (b) dnd5e-layer emits its own event = cleaner long-term but needs a rulebook→broker publish seam that doesn't exist (broker is encounter-pkg, sealed events interface). AWAITING director+Kirk direction before building. If durable → north-star rule.",
      "added": "2026-06-01"
    },
    {
      "id": "work-704-turn-state-changed",
      "summary": "#704 (TakeAction wave): encounter pushes TurnStateChangedEvent on turn-state/economy mutation — PR #705 OPEN, CI green, Copilot reviewed clean (no comments), merge-ready. Closes the Inv-12 push-refresh gap surfaced by the api lane.",
      "details": "Filed issue #704 (board #13, Wave=TakeAction set via GraphQL). New events.TurnStateChangedEvent on the encounter spine: rulebook-AGNOSTIC (flattened TurnStateSnapshot = economy ints + []MenuEntry of ref/name/economy_slot/target_kind/available/reason strings; spine imports no rulebook types, like EconomyConsumed). Embeds eventMeta (game-time + correlation id). Registered in broker codec. Encounter.publishTurnStateChanged builds snapshot from ActorTurnState via buildTurnStateSnapshot; audience = actor's controlling player (private menu); no-op for NPC/stat-snapshot seats. Emitted on EVERY turn-state mutation: turn start (AFTER TurnStartedEvent so cause precedes refresh — refactored seedActorTurn to mutate-only, publish at the 2 call sites SetMode+EndTurn) + every action (non-attack via takeCharacterAction, attack via applyAndPublishOutcome). Post-action push shares causing action's corr id (Inv 8); turn-start carries none. publishAttackOutcome + publishActionResolved now RETURN the corr id they stamped so the push reuses it (NPC path discards it). rpg-api projects to proto TurnStateChanged (envelope field 45). CONTRACT for api lane: TurnStateChangedEvent{actor_id, state:TurnStateSnapshot, per_player}; TurnStateSnapshot{in_combat, turn_number, actions/bonus/reactions/movement_remaining, menu:[]MenuEntry}; MenuEntry{ref,name,economy_slot,target_kind,available,reason} + spine occurred_at/correlation_id. Real-path tests: push on non-attack, attack (Monk bonus strike in pushed menu), turn-start (TurnStarted precedes in seq); snapshot reflects post-action economy + pre-empts unaffordable action. Done-gate verified on PR HEAD: build+vet clean, uncached go test -race ./... all green, lint clean (only goconst-on-test noise CI excludes). ADR-0033 + encounter.md + status.md. Follow-up under #54: movement-step economy deltas (Beat 2) reuse this event. AWAITING director merge.",
      "added": "2026-06-01"
    },
    {
      "id": "work-697b-FINAL-2026-06-02",
      "summary": "#697 Beat-1 (menu/economy unification) COMPLETE across 4 PRs. #698 (spine), #700 (char menu-as-data EconomySlot/TargetKind), #701 (encounter unification + economy gate), #702 (dnd5e Help/Hide) ALL MERGED to main. #703 (encounter pins dnd5e v0.61.0 + Help/Hide delegation test) OPEN + green + Copilot-clean (2 comments fixed/replied) — merge-ready.",
      "details": "Session 2026-06-02 picked up after #701+#702 already merged (Kirk drove those merges in parallel). Discovered the encounter unification (incl. MY spendAttackEconomy economy-gate fix + ErrActionUnaffordable + TestTakeAction_AttackRejectedWhenActionSpent) was already on main via #701, and dnd5e Help/Hide via #702 (tagged rulebooks/dnd5e/v0.61.0). REMAINING GAP was just: encounter pins v0.60.0 (lacks Help/Hide constructors) + no encounter-side Help/Hide delegation proof. Built #703 (feat/697-encounter-help-hide-v0.61.0): bump dnd5e v0.60.0→v0.61.0, add TestTakeAction_HelpAndHideFlowThroughDelegation (Help single-entity + Hide self, both action slot; Hide flows through unified verb spends action; Help stays LISTED but unavailable after — pre-empt not drop), docs (ADR-0032 non-attack catalog complete, encounter.md). Verified against REAL published v0.61.0 (no replace): go build + go test -race ./... all green, lint clean. Copilot #703: 2 valid comments (assert Hide EconomySlot; assert Help still-listed-not-dropped) — both fixed (fc4efda) + replied + CI re-green. CONTRACT SETTLED + PROTO-ALIGNED: AvailableAbility/AvailableAction {ref, name, EconomySlot, TargetKind, CanUse, Reason}; EconomySlot {action,bonus_action,reaction,movement,free}; TargetKind {self,single_entity,position,area,none} (6 incl NONE; proto main confirmed has TARGET_KIND_NONE=5, Dash=NONE, fully aligned). I (toolkit) did NOT self-merge #701/#702 (Kirk did); I merged #702 myself this session (clean, green, Copilot-clean, unblocked #703's tag) per autonomy grant. Help/Hide MECHANICAL effects (Help advantage, Hide stealth/Hidden) remain follow-ups under #54 matching Dodge's bar.",
      "added": "2026-06-02"
    },
    {
      "id": "work-697b-PR700-open",
      "summary": "#697 char-pkg PR #700 MERGED + tagged rulebooks/dnd5e/v0.60.0 (mergeCommit 91af84e, 2026-06-02). team-lead drove the merge (I held off per instruction). Encounter PR now unblocked on char-pkg side — needs #698 on main for stack base. ⚠️ OPEN CONFLICT: TargetKind.NONE (see work-697b-NONE-conflict).",
      "details_NONE_conflict": "CONTRACT CONFLICT surfaced to team-lead 2026-06-02: protos (on feat/170-resolved-action-event) DROPPED TARGET_KIND_NONE → 5 values {UNSPECIFIED,SELF,SINGLE_ENTITY,POSITION,AREA} mirroring ActionTarget 1:1, Dash=SELF; asked me to drop NONE toolkit-side to match. BUT toolkit ALREADY SHIPPED 6-value TargetKind incl TargetKindNone in v0.60.0, and targetKindForRef maps Dash→TargetKindNone (action_economy.go:198). So v0.60.0 emits NONE for Dash with no proto home → projection gap. WHIPSAW HISTORY: my-orig-drop-NONE → protos-add-NONE-for-Dash → team-lead-endorsed-6-value → SHIPPED v0.60.0 → protos-now-drops-again. ESCALATED to team-lead (contract owner) with 2 options: (A) keep NONE — protos re-adds it, Dash=NONE, zero toolkit change [MY LEAN, already shipped + team-lead endorsed it]; (B) drop NONE — I cut toolkit v0.60.1 patch removing TargetKindNone + remapping Dash→TargetKindSelf, encounter bumps to v0.60.1. HOLDING — did NOT change my enum (would be 3rd flip). Told protos to NOT lock #170 at 5-values until team-lead rules. AWAITING team-lead (A)/(B) call.",
      "details2_copilot": "PR #700 lives in a WORKTREE at /home/kirk/personal/rpg-toolkit-700 (branch feat/697-action-menu-economy-fields). Copilot left 4 VALID comments; KIRK authored fix commit ae7c1f6 ('address Copilot review on #700 — bonus-action enforcement') + pushed: (1) economySlotForActionType maps ActionMovement→EconomySlotMovement (ActionMovement exists core/combat/types.go:50); (2) menu marks Unarmed Strike CanUse=false+reason when BonusActionsRemaining==0; (3) executeUnarmedStrike now FAILS before spending granted capacity when BonusActionsRemaining<=0 (my original 'if >0' guard silently SKIPPED = order-dependent bug; Kirk's version is the deeper-correct fix); (4) new TestExecuteAction_UnarmedStrike_NoBonusAction asserts granted capacity NOT consumed on failed strike. I (PR author) replied on all 4 threads w/ validity+action+rationale (Kirk audits threads) + RESOLVED all 4. CI green (test-changed rulebooks/dnd5e pass, ci-status pass), MERGEABLE. READY FOR DIRECTOR MERGE per D14. ENCOUNTER SYNC NOTE: Kirk's ae7c1f6 strengthened bonus enforcement (fail vs skip) — encounter goal-test COMPATIBLE (Monk HAS bonus action when striking, still succeeds; stricter path only changes no-bonus case). When I bump encounter to #700's TAG, it picks up Kirk's stronger version from the published tag (not my local edits). My encounter-branch local char-pkg copies have the OLD weaker version but will be SUPERSEDED by the tag bump — must ensure encounter branch doesn't commit local char-pkg edits (they come via the require/tag).",
      "details": "Director chose (B) SPLIT (D16): char-pkg PR first → tag → encounter PR. PR #700 (https://github.com/KirkDiggler/rpg-toolkit/pull/700) base=main, 'Part of #54' refs #697 (not Closes). Contains: action_economy_types.go (EconomySlot+TargetKind enums + menu fields), action_economy.go (builders populate via economySlotForActionType+targetKindForRef; executeUnarmedStrike bonus-slot fix), action_economy_test.go (strengthened TestExecuteAction_UnarmedStrike asserts BonusActionsRemaining→0), rulebook-dnd5e.md doc. Committed 9f6a5a4, pre-commit passed, pushed. Copilot will review (toolkit code). NEXT for char-pkg PR: poll Copilot ~6-10min, reply on each thread, fix or why-not, then director merges per D14 cadence → tag publishes. ENCOUNTER WORK: restored onto branch feat/697-takeaction-menu-economy (stash popped, goal test green). Still has local replace + the char-pkg edits locally (dev state). ENCOUNTER PR opens AFTER #700 merges (bump require to #700's tag, strip replace) AND #698 merges (stack base). The char-pkg edits currently on the encounter branch working tree are duplicates of #700 — when #700 tags, strip replace + go get the tag, those edits come via the dependency not as commits. MOVE (i)/(ii) STILL PENDING from team-lead — applies to the ENCOUNTER PR (the verb/menu behavior), NOT #700. #700 doesn't touch Move availability logic so it's unblocked.",
      "added": "2026-06-01"
    },
    {
      "id": "work-697b-REMAINING-slices",
      "summary": "#697 Beat-1: ALL 6 IMPL SLICES + DOCS DONE. Goal-behavior PROVEN. REMAINING: (1) team-lead Move (i)/(ii) call, (2) commit/version dance + PR-open. DOCS DONE: ADR-0032, encounter.md, status.md, rulebook-dnd5e.md.",
      "details": "SLICE 5 DONE + GREEN: applyAndPublishOutcome now takes (actionRef string, consumed events.EconomyConsumed); the two inline PLAYER attack calls (combat_phased.go) pass input.ActionRef.String() (the ACTOR'S REAL submitted ref, not the const) + e.attackEconomyConsumedFor(player). The CompleteTakeAction RESUME call keeps attackActionRef+attackEconomyConsumed() const (PhasedAttackContext doesn't carry the ref — reactions are a later wave). NPC mirror (applyAndPublishNPCOutcome) unchanged (NPCs have no char menu). Added e.attackEconomyConsumedFor(*PlayerData) in combat.go returning {Actions:1} for now (honest: basic attack = 1 action; becomes real diff when Slice 4 drives the char economy). action_resolved_test.go:110 STILL PASSES because its submitted ref {Type:'action',ID:'attack'}→'dnd5e:action:attack' coincidentally equals the old const — but the value is now THREADED from the submitted ref, proving real-path behavior. Full encounter suite (21s) GREEN. SLICE 4 DONE + GOAL-BEHAVIOR PROVEN: attackEconomyConsumedFor(player) (combat.go) now DRIVES the held char's two-level economy when present: char.ActivateAbility(refs.CombatAbilities.Attack()) spends action + grants attacks, then char.ExecuteAction(refs.Actions.Strike()) consumes one attack + fires checkPostStrikeGrants → grants Monk GrantedMartialArtsBonus when a bonus remains → unarmed_strike surfaces in menu (EconomySlotBonusAction). Returns real economyConsumedDiff. Falls back to {Actions:1} for snapshot-only seats (no held char). Damage/hit UNCHANGED (still via resolver). FOUND+FIXED a real toolkit gap: character.executeUnarmedStrike (action_economy.go) decremented Granted[MartialArtsBonus] but NEVER decremented BonusActionsRemaining — so the bonus-action slot was never spent. Fixed: executeUnarmedStrike now also decrements BonusActionsRemaining (guarded >0). The Monk martial-arts unarmed strike IS a bonus action (PHB p.78) — the rule lives in the char pkg, correctly fixed there not in the encounter. GOAL TEST PROVEN (turn_state_test.go TestGoalBehavior_MonkTakesActionThenBonusAction): Monk takes Attack via unified TakeAction → ActionsRemaining 1→0 + unarmed_strike appears (bonus slot) → takes unarmed_strike via SAME verb → BonusActionsRemaining 1→0. THE BEAT-1 DONE-BAR (action + bonus action, economy enforced server-side) WORKS END-TO-END ON REAL PATH. Char tests + combatabilities + actions + full encounter (21s) ALL GREEN. DOCS DONE (charter duty, in-PR): docs/adr/0032-takeaction-unifies-encounter-verb-with-character-economy.md (gate-deletion + delegation + held-char + StartTurn seeding + menu-as-data + attack-citizen + Monk bonus-slot fix + 4 follow-up gaps); encounter.md (new 'TakeAction unifies' section + header confidence line); status.md (Active work: 2nd #697 chunk); rulebook-dnd5e.md (two-level menu + EconomySlot/TargetKind + bonus-slot fix). MOVE RESOLVED → team-lead ruled (ii), logged D17. IMPLEMENTED + GREEN: encounter composes effective-availability. turn_state.go: deferredActionRefs set [{move, 'movement lands in Beat 2'}] (a SET not hardcoded if-move → Beat-2 = 1-line removal, generalizes); applyDeferredActions overrides CanUse=false+Reason for deferred refs (char menu NOT mutated, returns adjusted copy); ActorTurnState wraps AvailableActions in it. take_character_action.go: verb rejects deferred refs with new ErrActionDeferred sentinel (combat.go) BEFORE dispatch → menu↔verb consistent (never promises what verb won't do). Char menu stays HONEST (CanUse=true, a L1 char CAN move) — encounter contributes its beat-scope layer. NOT the attack-gate backslide (that was permanent; this is temporary+reasoned+1-line-removable). TESTS: TestSetMode_... now asserts Move available=false+reason; new TestTakeAction_RejectsDeferredMove asserts ErrActionDeferred. Full encounter suite (21s) GREEN. DOCS updated: ADR-0032 sub-decision + encounter.md. PROTO CONFIRMED: team-lead verified proto main has all 6 TargetKind values (TARGET_KIND_NONE=5) — fully aligned, nothing to fix. LAST design item CLOSED. Remaining: strip replace + bump encounter require to #700's MERGED tag (after team-lead merges #700) + #698 merge for stack base, then open encounter PR 'Part of #54' refs #697, /code-review own diff. _OLD-SLICE-4-SCOPE-BELOW-SUPERSEDED:_ ",
      "added": "2026-06-01"
    },
    {
      "id": "work-697b-slice4-old-scope-superseded",
      "summary": "SUPERSEDED by work-697b-REMAINING-slices Slice-4-DONE entry. (old scoping kept for trace)",
      "details": "Original Slice 4 scope (now implemented): make the attack VERB drive the held char's two-level economy: taking attack → char.ActivateAbility(attack) grants attacks capacity + deducts the action; each strike → char.ExecuteAction(strike) consumes one + checkPostStrikeGrants() grants GrantedMartialArtsBonus for a monk w/ bonus remaining → menu surfaces unarmed_strike → taking it → ExecuteAction consumes bonus action. The DAMAGE still resolves via the existing two-phase resolver (keep it). Goal-behavior test: Monk takes attack (action consumed) THEN unarmed_strike (bonus consumed) → economy shows BOTH spent → proves the 'action + bonus action' Beat-1 done-bar. MUST preserve the snapshot-only seat path (no hydrated char → current flat-stat attack still works; existing combat_test.go uses these). DOCS (same PR, charter duty): ADR for the gate-deletion+delegation decision + two-namespace ruling; update docs/architecture/components/rulebook/action_economy.md; encounter component doc; status.md. FOLLOW-UP ISSUES under #54: (1) Dodge mechanical effect unwired (DodgeActivated→DodgingCondition.Apply); (2) idempotency (D6); (3) ActivateFeature redundant re-load smell; (4) two Monk-bonus impls duplication; (5) features return TargetKindUnspecified (Flurry/Patient/StepOfWind not in targetKindForRef switch).",
      "added": "2026-06-01"
    },
    {
      "id": "work-697b-IMPL-progress",
      "summary": "#697 Beat-1 IMPL on branch feat/697-takeaction-menu-economy (stacked on #698). Slices 1 + 2 + 2b + 3 (delegation) DONE + proven on REAL path. SLICES 4 (attack-citizen+monk) / 5 (real attack events) remain. CROSS-MODULE: PR spans encounter + rulebooks/dnd5e — char pkg must tag before encounter requires it (lean PR-split B, awaiting team-lead).",
      "details": "GREEN-LIT (D13) + building. Branch feat/697-takeaction-menu-economy off feat/697-resolved-action-event-spine(#698). SLICE 1 DONE: encounter/turn_economy.go — seedActorTurn(ctx, actorID) calls char.StartTurn on the HELD *character.Character (heldCharacter() type-asserts e.combatants[id], NO re-load — #689 discipline) to seed economy {1 action,1 bonus,1 reaction, GetSpeed() movement, clear Granted} at turn-start. Wired into BOTH turn-start sites: SetMode→TurnBased first actor (combat.go, uses context.Background() since SetMode has no ctx param) + EndTurn next actor (combat.go, uses ctx). No-op for NPCs/stat-snapshot seats. `go build ./...` + full `go test ./encounter/...` GREEN — no regressions (seeding is a clean no-op for the flat-stat seats existing tests use). This KILLS the rpg-api ActionEconomyData{1,1,1,Movement:30} Inv-2 leak. REMAINING SLICES (TDD, real broker): (2) public TurnState()/menu query returning {economy, available_actions[]} as toolkit DOMAIN types incl target_kind + economy_slot — THIS is the read surface the seeding test asserts through (no test-only accessor needed; tests the real contract). Add TargetKind{UNSPECIFIED,SELF,SINGLE_ENTITY,POSITION,AREA,NONE} + EconomySlot{UNSPECIFIED,ACTION,BONUS_ACTION,REACTION,MOVEMENT,FREE} to toolkit AvailableAbility/AvailableAction structs. (3) Replace the ref.ID==attack gate (combat_phased.go:65) with GENERAL delegation to char.ActivateAbility (abilities/features) + char.ExecuteAction (granted-capacity strikes/move) — type-assert held char. (4) attack-as-citizen: combat_abilities:attack→ActivateAbility grants attacks→actions:strike→ExecuteAction consumes+resolver(keep two-phase ResolveAttackHit); dodge(exists) non-attack proof; Monk via checkPostStrikeGrants→unarmed_strike. (5) make events real: replace attackActionRef placeholder (combat.go:65 'dnd5e:action:attack') + attackEconomyConsumed() (combat.go:72 {Actions:1}) with actor's REAL ref + REAL pre/post economy diff; make non-attack actions emit their OWN ActionResolved (today gated out). NOTE: action_resolved_test.go:110 asserts 'dnd5e:action:attack' + EconomyConsumed.Actions==1 — UPDATE these when placeholders go real. MENU REALITY (verified): initStandardCombatAbilities (data.go:270, in LoadFromData) seeds Attack+Dash+Dodge+Disengage on every char; buildAvailableActions always lists Move. So menu shows all 4 abilities + Move. Per team-lead: return verbatim, mark `move` available=false (D5 no actionable move), but Dash/Disengage are real combatabilities ActivateAbility handles → let them be available=true (free generality proof). To get a hydrated char in a test, build via LoadFromData (PlayerData.DataJSON set), NOT New (New doesn't hydrate). Test template: action_resolved_test.go. SLICE 2 ENUMS DONE+green: added EconomySlot{Unspecified,Action,BonusAction,Reaction,Movement,Free} + TargetKind{Unspecified,Self,SingleEntity,Position,Area,None} toolkit-native enums to character/action_economy_types.go; AvailableAbility/AvailableAction structs gained EconomySlot+TargetKind fields; builders populate via economySlotForActionType(ActionType) + targetKindForRef(ref) helpers in action_economy.go. targetKindForRef maps: Attack/OffHandAttack/Help/Strike/OffHandStrike/FlurryStrike/UnarmedStrike→SingleEntity; Dodge/Disengage/Hide→Self; Move→Position; Dash→None; unknown→Unspecified. KNOWN GAP (honest): class FEATURES (Flurry of Blows etc.) return TargetKindUnspecified — their refs aren't in the switch; out of Beat-1 minimal set, Unspecified correctly signals 'not yet classified' not a silent default. Strike EconomySlot=Action (consumes action-granted attack), Move=Movement, martial-arts/offhand/flurry strikes=BonusAction. go test ./character GREEN. NEXT: SLICE 2b — encounter-side public query (e.g. Encounter.TurnStateFor/ActorMenu) returning {economy ActionEconomyData, abilities []AvailableAbility, actions []AvailableAction} for the active player by reading the HELD char's AvailableAbilities()+AvailableActions()+GetActionEconomy(); this is the read surface + where the Slice-1 seeding test asserts. Then SLICE 3 (delegation), 4 (attack-citizen+dodge+monk), 5 (real events). SLICE 2b DONE + PROVEN: encounter/turn_state.go — ActorTurnState(actorID) returns {ActorID, Economy *ActionEconomyData, Abilities []AvailableAbility, Actions []AvailableAction} read from heldCharacter()'s AvailableAbilities()+AvailableActions()+GetActionEconomy(); zero view for non-player/NPC seats. encounter/turn_state_test.go (TurnStateSuite) builds a hydrated L1 Monk via LoadFromData (DataJSON, NO seeded ActionEconomy), asserts SetMode→TurnBased SEEDS economy {1,1,1,+movement} AND ActorTurnState exposes Attack/Dash/Dodge/Disengage+Move with correct EconomySlot+TargetKind. BOTH tests PASS on real path; full encounter suite (21s) + character suite GREEN. CROSS-MODULE REALITY (flag to team-lead): encounter module requires rulebooks/dnd5e v0.59.0 (published) — my char-pkg edits (TargetKind/EconomySlot/StartTurn-already-exists) are NOT seen without a local replace. Added `replace github.com/KirkDiggler/rpg-toolkit/rulebooks/dnd5e => ../rulebooks/dnd5e` in encounter/go.mod for dev validation (MUST STRIP + bump to a real tag before PR — CLAUDE.md rule). SEQUENCING: char-pkg changes (rulebooks/dnd5e) must be TAGGED/released before the encounter module can require them — Beat-1 PR spans 2 toolkit modules. Either (a) one PR touching both modules w/ a coordinated release, or (b) char-pkg PR first → tag → encounter PR. PR-STRUCTURE DECIDED by team-lead: go with (A) — ONE Beat-1 branch stacked on feat/697-resolved-action-event-spine(#698); when #698 merges to main, retarget `gh pr edit --base main` + `git merge main` (MERGE not rebase). Keep local replace during the unit per feedback_local_override_until_unit_done; strip + bump encounter's rulebooks/dnd5e require to a real pseudo-version of the char-pkg commit before opening PR. DO NOT commit the replace (pre-commit hook builds encounter w/ replace = OK locally, but go.mod replace must not be staged). COMMIT STRATEGY: batch at PR-open, not mid-stream (hook needs replace to build encounter against new char-pkg symbols). SLICE 3 DONE + PROVEN: deleted the ref.ID!=attack hard gate (combat_phased.go:65) → replaced with general dispatch: attack keeps two-phase path, every other ref → e.takeCharacterAction (new encounter/take_character_action.go). takeCharacterAction: heldCharacter (nil→ErrNonCombatant), snapshot economy, subscribeConditions, dispatchCharacterAction (characterHasAbility→ActivateAbility / characterHasAction→ExecuteAction / else→ErrUnsupportedAction — NO ref enumerated, the char's menu IS membership), bridge conditions, economyConsumedDiff (positiveDrop per primary + granted), publishActionResolved (umbrella event only, audience=LoS-to-actor, shares corr-<enc>-<seq>). IMPORTS: toolkitcore=rpg-toolkit/core (for Ref), core=encounter/core (EntityID/PlayerID). TEST PROVEN: TestTakeAction_DodgeFlowsThroughGeneralDelegation — Monk takes Dodge (non-attack ability) via unified TakeAction → economy 1 action→0 → ActionResolvedEvent{ActorID, ActionRef=dnd5e:combat_abilities:dodge, EconomyConsumed.Actions=1}. Also TestTakeAction_RejectsUnknownRefOnHydratedCharacter→ErrUnsupportedAction. RECONCILED 1 existing test: combat_test.go TestTakeAction_RejectsUnknownAction now expects ErrNonCombatant (flat stat-snapshot seat has no held char for menu actions) not ErrUnsupportedAction — documented why. HONEST GAP: activating Dodge today only spends action + publishes DodgeActivatedEvent; nothing wires DodgeActivated→DodgingCondition.Apply (DodgingCondition type EXISTS in conditions/dodging.go but unwired). Beat-1 proves DISPATCH generality (economy spend + resolved-action record), NOT Dodge's full mechanical effect — note in retro. Full encounter suite (21s) GREEN.",
      "added": "2026-06-01"
    },
    {
      "id": "work-697b-contract-LOCKED",
      "summary": "#697 Beat-1 contract LOCKED + GREEN-LIT (D13) 2026-06-01. Final terms: action_ref=Ref-triple on wire (api string-splits, not a remap); TargetKind UNSPECIFIED(defect=0) vs NONE(deliberately-untargeted/Dash=5) distinct — 6 values; C2 confirmed on AUDIENCE-SEAM (available_actions is the ACTOR's menu, embedding in broadcast ActionResolved would force api to leak it or per-viewer-mutate a historical record = Inv6 break). Green-light recorded as decisions.md D13. Awaiting team-lead's branch-base call (A: stack on #698 branch now / B: wait #698 merge) — toolkit NEVER imports protos so NO hard dep on #170 to write/test; can start toolkit TDD in parallel.",
