ons emit their OWN ActionResolved (today gated out). NOTE: action_resolved_test.go:110 asserts 'dnd5e:action:attack' + EconomyConsumed.Actions==1 — UPDATE these when placeholders go real. MENU REALITY (verified): initStandardCombatAbilities (data.go:270, in LoadFromData) seeds Attack+Dash+Dodge+Disengage on every char; buildAvailableActions always lists Move. So menu shows all 4 abilities + Move. Per team-lead: return verbatim, mark `move` available=false (D5 no actionable move), but Dash/Disengage are real combatabilities ActivateAbility handles → let them be available=true (free generality proof). To get a hydrated char in a test, build via LoadFromData (PlayerData.DataJSON set), NOT New (New doesn't hydrate). Test template: action_resolved_test.go. SLICE 2 ENUMS DONE+green: added EconomySlot{Unspecified,Action,BonusAction,Reaction,Movement,Free} + TargetKind{Unspecified,Self,SingleEntity,Position,Area,None} toolkit-native enums to character/action_economy_types.go; AvailableAbility/AvailableAction structs gained EconomySlot+TargetKind fields; builders populate via economySlotForActionType(ActionType) + targetKindForRef(ref) helpers in action_economy.go. targetKindForRef maps: Attack/OffHandAttack/Help/Strike/OffHandStrike/FlurryStrike/UnarmedStrike→SingleEntity; Dodge/Disengage/Hide→Self; Move→Position; Dash→None; unknown→Unspecified. KNOWN GAP (honest): class FEATURES (Flurry of Blows etc.) return TargetKindUnspecified — their refs aren't in the switch; out of Beat-1 minimal set, Unspecified correctly signals 'not yet classified' not a silent default. Strike EconomySlot=Action (consumes action-granted attack), Move=Movement, martial-arts/offhand/flurry strikes=BonusAction. go test ./character GREEN. NEXT: SLICE 2b — encounter-side public query (e.g. Encounter.TurnStateFor/ActorMenu) returning {economy ActionEconomyData, abilities []AvailableAbility, actions []AvailableAction} for the active player by reading the HELD char's AvailableAbilities()+AvailableActions(