t go.mod replace must not be staged). COMMIT STRATEGY: batch at PR-open, not mid-stream (hook needs replace to build encounter against new char-pkg symbols). SLICE 3 DONE + PROVEN: deleted the ref.ID!=attack hard gate (combat_phased.go:65) → replaced with general dispatch: attack keeps two-phase path, every other ref → e.takeCharacterAction (new encounter/take_character_action.go). takeCharacterAction: heldCharacter (nil→ErrNonCombatant), snapshot economy, subscribeConditions, dispatchCharacterAction (characterHasAbility→ActivateAbility / characterHasAction→ExecuteAction / else→ErrUnsupportedAction — NO ref enumerated, the char's menu IS membership), bridge conditions, economyConsumedDiff (positiveDrop per primary + granted), publishActionResolved (umbrella event only, audience=LoS-to-actor, shares corr-<enc>-<seq>). IMPORTS: toolkitcore=rpg-toolkit/core (for Ref), core=encounter/core (EntityID/PlayerID). TEST PROVEN: TestTakeAction_DodgeFlowsThroughGeneralDelegation — Monk takes Dodge (non-attack ability) via unified TakeAction → economy 1 action→0 → ActionResolvedEvent{ActorID, ActionRef=dnd5e:combat_abilities:dodge, EconomyConsumed.Actions=1}. Also TestTakeAction_RejectsUnknownRefOnHydratedCharacter→ErrUnsupportedAction. RECONCILED 1 existing test: combat_test.go TestTakeAction_RejectsUnknownAction now expects ErrNonCombatant (flat stat-snapshot seat has no held char for menu actions) not ErrUnsupportedAction — documented why. HONEST GAP: activating Dodge today only spends action + publishes DodgeActivatedEvent; nothing wires DodgeActivated→DodgingCondition.Apply (DodgingCondition type EXISTS in conditions/dodging.go but unwired). Beat-1 proves DISPATCH generality (economy spend + resolved-action record), NOT Dodge's full mechanical effect — note in retro. Full encounter suite (21s) GREEN.",
